    These terms apply to your use of this website, including the Nexus documentation on it (together, the "site"). The
    site is run by Airogine ("we", "us"). By using the site, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't
    use it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="nexus-software">The Nexus software</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover the website, not the Nexus software. Downloading, installing or using Nexus is governed by the
    license agreement that comes with it, or by your agreement with Airogine or the integrator you bought it from. If
    one of those agreements conflicts with these terms, the agreement applies to the software.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">Using the site</h2>
  <p>You may use the site to learn about Nexus, evaluate it, and install, run and support it. Please don't:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the site in a way that breaks the law or infringes anyone's rights;</li>
    <li>try to get into parts of the site or its systems you aren't meant to, or test their security without our written permission;</li>
    <li>disrupt the site, overload it, or get around measures that protect it;</li>
    <li>copy the site in bulk or use automated tools to scrape it, except search engines indexing it in the usual way;</li>
    <li>send us anything misleading through the demo form, or someone else's details without their permission.</li>
  </ul>

